Yes, this is the same character who had a near-YASD experience. No, he 
didn't drop the Amulet on the high altar... :-)

Cohen followed fairly typical Barbarian behaviour, i.e. whacking 
monsters until they died. He picked up some nice armor from the mines, 
dwarfish mithril, +2 iron shoes, +1 dwarfish helm. Sokoban had an AoR. 
Deep in the mines Cohen found the remains of Rincewind the Wizzard, who 
had a CoMR, BoH (cursed) and a magic lamp. He found two more magic lamps 
elsewhere in the mines.

At Mines' End, Cohen quaffed a smoky !oOD and a djinni offered him a 
wish. Cohen opted for GoP. Then came the unfortunate incident in the 
Bigroom, where Cohen contracted food poisoning (he meant to eat a blue 
dragon). Cohen saved his butt with a wished-for blessed unicorn horn. He 
then ate the blue dragon and made scale mail from the scales (3 extra AC 
points).

Cohen continued through the dungeon, #twoweaponing dwarfish short 
swords. On level 20 he found a double bones file - nothing much 
remarkable, SDSM, a bunch of scrolls, wands and potions, plus Excalibur 
(which was tossed into Cohen's BoH). Cohen skipped Medusa's and went to 
the Castle, played with the drawbridge (that's so much fun!) and grabbed 
the /oW (0:2). Two b?oC (got one), speed boots, helm of telepathy, holy 
water and a wand of cancellation. Cohen finally got some holy water and 
blessed and enchanted some of his gear. He quaffed a !oGL to reach level 
14, and prepared for the Quest.

Before the Quest, Cohen took a trip to level 4 to buy a tinning kit, but 
the shopkeeper didn't like invisible customers, so he dug his way in. 
Kit purchased, he headed off to grab the Bell, oh, and some trinket that 
Pelias wanted back. Cohen put Thoth Amon to sleep, killed him, and 
retreived the loot. Pelias decided he didn't really want the trinket 
after all, so Cohen took it with him.

Cohen still didn't have fire, cold or sleep resistance, so he looked for 
the portal to Ludios. He got there, acquired cold and sleep resistance, 
then decided to go to Gehennom anyway. He wrote a stack of magic maps 
and headed off. Asmo and Baal got paid off, Juiblex was killed, Orcus 
was rubber-chickened. Cohen found a ring of fire resistance, then got 
the intrinsic from a hell hound in Vlad's Tower. Vlad managed to drain a 
level from Cohen before crumbling.

Cohen continued down, found the VS, went back up. Rodney was very 
persistent: it took six tries to kill him with a /oD. Cohen headed back 
to the square, did the invocation, hacked his way through the Sanctum, 
got the Amulet, went back up. The mysterious force threw him back a lot 
in the deeper levels, but he got through the higher levels fairly 
easily. Rodney showed up by his Tower, then double-troubled at the Castle.

Before the planes, Cohen wrote a couple of ?oGD and promoted some 
potions from healing to extra healing. On Earth, Rodney went down for 
the fifth time. Cohen used his solitary spell - light, which he had 
never cast - with his ?oGD to locate the portals. He went through the 
planes with minimal trouble. On Astral, he showed up on the right. Door 
#3 had Death behind it, who cost Cohen 28 HPs before he went down. The 
altar was lawful, so Cohen turned back. Pesty was behind Door #2, he 
made Cohen sick, but Cohen used his u-horn. He slipped past the 
monsters, and reached the altar, which was neutral.

Crom did his bit with the choir, et al, and Cohen became a Demigod.

